 <name>scope</name>
 <channel>pecl.php.net</channel>
 <summary>Scope: the identity of the operation (request, job) that code belongs to</summary>
 <description>The Scope class proposed in the PHP RFC "Scope", for PHP 8.2 and later. Fibers and generators belong to the scope current at their creation; Scope::getRootScope() is the scope outside any Scope::run().</description>
 <lead>
  <name>Frode Børli</name>
  <user>frodeborli</user>
  <email>frode@ennerd.com</email>
  <active>yes</active>
 </lead>
 <date>2026-10-27</date>
 <version>
  <release>0.4.3</release>
  <api>0.4.0</api>
 </version>
 <stability>
  <release>alpha</release>
  <api>alpha</api>
 </stability>
 <license uri="https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT">MIT</license>
 <notes>0.4.3: builds and works on ZTS PHP (it did not compile there): ext/session's globals and the locale ini entry are reached per thread, and the session and locale follow the scope on ZTS too; thread tests with the parallel extension, and ZTS builds in CI. unset() of a superglobal inside a scope no longer removes it from every other scope. Switching scopes is cheaper: a superglobal that both scopes leave empty is not moved, nor is the session when neither scope has one, and the C-side copies of the request arrays are updated without feeding the cycle collector, which made it run every 10000 switches (a fiber resumed in another scope went from about 322 ns to about 260 ns).</notes>
